[size=5][b]SmoothCam - BoD Edition[/b][/size]
[i]A third-person camera that trails your character instead of being bolted to it.[/i]

I'm a hobbyist software engineer, and I like building small utilities that other people end up finding useful. This one started with the camera in The Blood of Dawnwalker. It follows the character almost rigidly, so every step, stop and landing hits the view at once, and a few hours in I missed the softer follow I knew from SmoothCam in Skyrim. So I wrote one for this game.

With the mod, the camera trails a little behind your character and catches up smoothly, with separate rates for horizontal and vertical movement. Turning is left alone: only the follow lags, so looking around feels the same as before. While you aim, the trail eases down to 30% so the view stays on your crosshair, and it eases back when you lower the weapon. Near walls the camera pulls in the way the game's own does. After a cutscene, a load or a teleport it snaps to your character instead of gliding across the map.

It also sets where the camera sits, separately for exploring, sprinting, combat and focus, aiming, and claw ride and anti-grav. Each one gets its own distance, height, shoulder offset and field of view. Settings live in an ini file, or on an in-game page if you also run [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/271]Dawnwalker Mod Menu[/url]. Either way, changes apply while the game runs.

[size=4][b]Presets and keys[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]V[/font]: move the camera to the other shoulder. It glides across in half a second.
[*]Presets: pick one on the Mod Menu page or with [font=Courier New]preset[/font] in the ini. [b]Tight[/b] barely trails, with the camera a little closer. [b]Balanced[/b] is the default: a clear trail that settles fast, with the camera where the game puts it. [b]Cinematic[/b] is a heavy, slow trail with smoothed turning, the camera a little further back and higher, and a wider view when you sprint. Your ten save slots come after them, then any presets you installed from other authors.
[*]On and off: the [font=Courier New]enabled[/font] switch, on the same page or in the ini. Off is the game's own camera: no follow and no camera position changes.
[/list]
SmoothCam binds only one key by default, so it doesn't eat into your keyboard. If you want a key to cycle presets or switch the mod on and off, set [font=Courier New]preset_key[/font] or [font=Courier New]toggle_key[/font] in the ini.
A short banner at the top of the screen names the preset, or says On or Off. Quick presses show one banner with the last name. A preset carries the follow feel, turning, the snap thresholds and the whole camera position (distance, height, shoulder offset and field of view per situation, plus the look limits). It leaves the on/off switches, the shoulder side, the aiming setting, banners and keys alone. All three keys can be changed in the ini, and a blank one is left unbound.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]UE4SS, one of these two. Both run UE4SS commit 97b7e501, which the DLL is built against. C++ mods only load on the UE4SS they were built for.
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/18]UE4SS for Dawnwalker[/url] by Vercadi, file [font=Courier New]Dawnwalker-UE4SS-v1.2.1-rc6-build25232147[/font] (version 1.3 on that page).
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/283]UE4SS for BoD[/url] by Framecore, version 2b, in either its Performance or its Compatibility profile.
[/list]
[*]The Steam version of the game, build 25232147.
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/271]Dawnwalker Mod Menu[/url] for the in-game settings page.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]1)[/b] Close the game.
[b]2)[/b] Extract the archive into the folder that contains the [i]ue4ss[/i] folder and [font=Courier New]Dawnwalker.exe[/font]:
[code]<Steam library>\steamapps\common\The Blood of Dawnwalker\Dawnwalker\Binaries\Win64[/code]
[b]3)[/b] Start the game. The archive carries the folder path, so the mod lands in [font=Courier New]ue4ss\Mods\DWSmoothCam[/font] by itself. There is no [font=Courier New]mods.txt[/font] edit: [font=Courier New]enabled.txt[/font] in the mod folder switches it on.

[font=Courier New]UE4SS.log[/font] shows these two lines when it loaded:
[code][DWSmoothCam] v0.8.0 loaded, on
[DWSmoothCam] GetCameraView hooked (slot 214)[/code]

To uninstall, close the game and delete [font=Courier New]ue4ss\Mods\DWSmoothCam[/font]. Nothing is written to save games. The camera changes live in memory and are gone on the next launch.

[b]Settings in game.[/b] With [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/271]Dawnwalker Mod Menu[/url] installed, SmoothCam gets its own page under Mod Settings, in the main menu and in the pause menu. It covers every setting except the three key bindings. The Preset entry at the top shows which preset your settings match, or Custom. Pick another and press Apply to load it. A change takes effect within a quarter second of Apply, with no restart.

[b]Settings without the Mod Menu.[/b] Edit [font=Courier New]config\smoothcam.ini[/font] in the mod folder. Save the file and look back at the game: changes apply within a quarter second. Key bindings are the exception, they are read when the game starts.

[b]Common issues[/b]
[list]
[*]The mod supports Steam build 25232147 only. On any other build it refuses to hook the camera and stays inactive, and [font=Courier New]UE4SS.log[/font] says so: [font=Courier New]unsupported game build, mod inactive[/font]. I would rather it do nothing than crash your game after a patch.
[*]After loading a preset from the Mod Menu, the open page still shows the old slider values until you reopen it, and refuses another Apply until then.
[*]The shoulder key and the preset key are ignored while the game is paused, including with the Mod Menu open, and while the mod is switched off. The on/off key works at any time, and the Mod Menu page shows its state.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Conflicts with any other mod that replaces the third-person camera. Run one or the other.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/350]FreeCam - UE4SS[/url] ([font=Courier New]F7[/font]) works alongside it. When you leave the free camera, the game camera snaps back to your character.
[*]Framecore's UE4SS in Compatibility mode logs [font=Courier New]A callback for 'LoadMap' must return bool or nil[/font] on each load and one [font=Courier New]bad conversion[/font] at startup. Both come from UE4SS's bundled BPModLoaderMod and ConsoleEnablerMod, not from SmoothCam.
[*]Keys: SmoothCam uses only [font=Courier New]V[/font] by default, which this game leaves unbound. P, F5 and F9 are used by the game.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Performance[/b][/size]
A camera mod that costs frames is not worth running, so I measured this one. The camera math runs once per frame inside the game's camera update and takes 3.3 to 3.6 microseconds, measured at 47 and 57 fps, standing and moving. That is about 0.02% of a 21 ms frame. A whole-frame A/B with UEBench (four 20-second captures, alternating on and off at the same spot) found no measurable difference: median frame times of 21.19 ms on and 21.22 ms off, a gap smaller than the spread between two captures in the same state, and no stutters either way.

Switching presets or shoulders is free as well. Eight presses inside one 20-second capture left the worst frame at 23 ms against an 18 ms average, with no stutters.

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size] ([font=Courier New]config\smoothcam.ini[/font] in the mod folder)
[spoiler]
[b]Keys[/b] (read at game start; any UE4SS key name)
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]toggle_key =[/font], [font=Courier New]preset_key =[/font] (blank, no key), [font=Courier New]shoulder_key = V[/font]
[/list]
[b]Follow[/b] (in presets, except enabled and aiming_follow)
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]enabled = 1[/font]: 0 is the game's own camera: no follow, no camera position changes, and the preset and shoulder keys do nothing.
[*][font=Courier New]follow_rate_h = 8[/font], [font=Courier New]follow_rate_v = 10[/font]: catch-up rate per second, horizontal and vertical. Higher is tighter.
[*][font=Courier New]curve_h = 2[/font], [font=Courier New]curve_v = 0[/font]: 0 constant, 1 linear, 2 smoothstep, 3 ease in-out. The curves start gently and reach full rate at [font=Courier New]catchup_distance = 150[/font] cm; [font=Courier New]min_rate_scale = 0.35[/font] is the rate at zero lag.
[*][font=Courier New]max_lag_h = 70[/font], [font=Courier New]max_lag_v = 50[/font]: the furthest the camera may fall behind, in cm.
[*][font=Courier New]soft_leash = 1[/font]: eases into the lag limit instead of stopping hard at it.
[*][font=Courier New]aiming_follow = 30[/font]: percent of the trail and the turning smoothing kept while you aim. 0 locks the camera to your aim, 100 trails as everywhere else. Not part of a preset.
[*][font=Courier New]rotation_smoothing = 0[/font], [font=Courier New]rotation_rate = 20[/font]: smooth turning too, and how fast it catches up.
[*][font=Courier New]wall_clamp = 1[/font]: keeps the smoothed camera in front of walls the game pulled its camera in for.
[/list]
[b]Safety and display[/b] (the two thresholds are in presets)
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]reset_distance = 500[/font]: cm moved in one frame that counts as a teleport and snaps the camera.
[*][font=Courier New]reset_gap = 0.25[/font]: seconds without camera updates (cutscene, free camera, load) before a snap.
[*][font=Courier New]show_banner = 1[/font]: the preset and on/off banner.
[*][font=Courier New]log_stats = 0[/font]: 1 writes smoothing statistics and the per-frame cost to [font=Courier New]UE4SS.log[/font] every 5 seconds.
[/list]
[b]Camera position[/b] (100 / 0 / 0 / 0 is the game as shipped; in presets except the two switches)
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]camera_tuning = 1[/font]: 0 puts every camera mode back as the game ships it.
[*]Per group, with the prefix [font=Courier New]exploration_[/font], [font=Courier New]sprint_[/font], [font=Courier New]combat_[/font], [font=Courier New]aiming_[/font] or [font=Courier New]traversal_[/font]: [font=Courier New]distance[/font] (% of the game's, 50 to 250), [font=Courier New]height[/font] (cm), [font=Courier New]shoulder[/font] (cm further out; centered cameras stay centered; not for traversal), [font=Courier New]fov[/font] (degrees added).
[*][font=Courier New]game_lag_scale = 3[/font]: multiplies the game's own camera lag speeds. The game lags its camera a little by itself, and two lags stacked feel mushy. Higher makes the game's part tighter, so SmoothCam's follow is the one you feel. 1 is the game's own.
[*][font=Courier New]shoulder_swap = 0[/font]: 1 is the other shoulder. [font=Courier New]V[/font] switches it.
[*][font=Courier New]position_transition = 0.5[/font]: seconds a position change or shoulder swap glides over. 0 snaps.
[*][font=Courier New]pitch_min = -60[/font], [font=Courier New]pitch_max = 40[/font]: look down and up limits while exploring, sprinting and in focus. Aiming and combat already allow -89 / 89.
[/list]
[b]Presets[/b]: [font=Courier New]preset = 102[/font] shows the matching preset (0 Custom, 101 Tight, 102 Balanced, 103 Cinematic, 1 to 10 a slot, 201 and up an installed preset); change it to load one. [font=Courier New]preset_save[/font] (1 to 10) saves to a slot and the mod sets it back to 0. The mod writes these, and key presses that change them, back to the ini only while you play, never behind an open Mod Menu page. Saved slots go to [font=Courier New]config\presets\Slot N.ini[/font]; the mod creates the folder.
[/spoiler]

[size=4][b]For mod authors: making a preset[/b][/size]
[spoiler]
If you land on a camera you like, share it. The optional file [b]SmoothCam Example Preset[/b] (Files tab) installs one preset, Over the Shoulder, with every key commented: range, default and what it does. It is the quickest template to copy.

A preset is one [b].ini[/b] file in [i]ue4ss\Mods\DWSmoothCam\config\presets[/i]. SmoothCam reads that folder when the game starts, lists each file in V's cycle after the player's own slots, and adds it to the Preset entry on the Mod Menu page under its name.

[b]1)[/b] Set the camera up in game, from the Mod Menu or the ini.
[b]2)[/b] On the SmoothCam page, pick a slot under Save current settings to and press Apply. This writes [i]presets\Slot N.ini[/i] with every setting a preset carries.
[b]3)[/b] Copy that file and give the copy a name of your own, for example [i]presets\YourName - Low Chase.ini[/i]. Do not name it [b]Slot 1.ini[/b] to [b]Slot 10.ini[/b]: those are the player's save slots, and the mod overwrites them.
[b]4)[/b] Change the [b]name[/b] line. That text is what the banner and the Mod Menu show. Comments starting with [b];[/b] stay in the file, since the mod never rewrites a preset it did not save.
[b]5)[/b] Restart the game. The preset appears after the slots.

[code]; Low Chase by YourName
name = Low Chase
follow_rate_h = 5
follow_rate_v = 6
max_lag_h = 110
exploration_distance = 120
exploration_height = -20
exploration_fov = 5[/code]

[b]Rules[/b]
[list]
[*]One [b]key = value[/b] per line. A preset may list only the keys it wants to change; loading it leaves every other setting as the player has it.
[*][b]name[/b]: up to 48 bytes. The characters [b]|[/b], [b];[/b] and [b]#[/b] cannot appear in it. Without a name line the file name is used.
[*]Values outside a setting's range are clamped to the range, and 0/1 settings treat anything but 0 as 1.
[*]Keys that are not listed below are ignored, so a preset cannot change the on/off switches, the shoulder side, the aiming setting, banners or key bindings.
[*]Up to 50 presets in the folder are used, in file-name order. Files over 64 KB, or without a single preset key, are skipped. [font=Courier New]UE4SS.log[/font] lists each preset it loaded.
[/list]

[b]Keys[/b] (range, shipped default)
[list]
[*]Follow: [font=Courier New]follow_rate_h[/font] and [font=Courier New]follow_rate_v[/font] (0.5 to 30, 8 and 10), [font=Courier New]curve_h[/font] and [font=Courier New]curve_v[/font] (0 constant, 1 linear, 2 smoothstep, 3 ease in-out; 2 and 0), [font=Courier New]catchup_distance[/font] (10 to 500 cm, 150), [font=Courier New]min_rate_scale[/font] (0.05 to 1, 0.35), [font=Courier New]max_lag_h[/font] (0 to 300 cm, 70), [font=Courier New]max_lag_v[/font] (0 to 200 cm, 50), [font=Courier New]soft_leash[/font] (0 or 1, 1)
[*]Turning and walls: [font=Courier New]rotation_smoothing[/font] (0 or 1, 0), [font=Courier New]rotation_rate[/font] (1 to 60, 20), [font=Courier New]wall_clamp[/font] (0 or 1, 1)
[*]Snaps: [font=Courier New]reset_distance[/font] (100 to 3000 cm, 500), [font=Courier New]reset_gap[/font] (0.05 to 2 s, 0.25)
[*]Camera, all modes: [font=Courier New]game_lag_scale[/font] (1 to 20, 3), [font=Courier New]position_transition[/font] (0 to 2 s, 0.5), [font=Courier New]pitch_min[/font] (-89 to -30, -60), [font=Courier New]pitch_max[/font] (20 to 89, 40)
[*]Per situation, with the prefix [font=Courier New]exploration_[/font], [font=Courier New]sprint_[/font], [font=Courier New]combat_[/font], [font=Courier New]aiming_[/font] or [font=Courier New]traversal_[/font]: [font=Courier New]distance[/font] (50 to 250 %, 100), [font=Courier New]height[/font] (-50 to 100 cm, 0), [font=Courier New]shoulder[/font] (-60 to 100 cm, 0; not for traversal), [font=Courier New]fov[/font] (-30 to 30 degrees, 0)
[/list]

[b]Sharing a preset on Nexus[/b]
Pack the file with its folder path, [i]ue4ss\Mods\DWSmoothCam\config\presets\YourName - Low Chase.ini[/i], so players extract it into [i]Dawnwalker\Binaries\Win64[/i] as they did SmoothCam. List SmoothCam as a requirement. Give the file a name no other preset is likely to use; a file with the same name replaces the other on extract.
[/spoiler]

[size=4][b]Source and bug reports[/b][/size]
The source is on [url=https://github.com/littleRabbit94/dawnwalker-smoothcam]GitHub[/url], with a design document that covers how the camera hook works and everything I measured along the way. If something looks wrong, a post with the DWSmoothCam lines from your [font=Courier New]UE4SS.log[/font], your game build and which UE4SS package you run is usually enough for me to find it.

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]
Built on [url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS]UE4SS[/url] by the UE4SS-RE team (MIT). Runs on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/18]Vercadi's[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/283]Framecore's[/url] UE4SS packages for this game, and the settings page exists thanks to [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/271]Dawnwalker Mod Menu[/url]. GPL-3.0-or-later, included in the archive. Inspired by SmoothCam for Skyrim; not affiliated with it or its author.
